 "notes": "Two OCR sheets: sheet 1 has interleaved text columns, tables 1-3 and three cross sections; sheet 2 has graphic lithologic logs. Informal units Q1-Q6, Tp, Tu recorded with ages and correlations from the text; facies suffixes b (beach), l (backbarrier), o (offshore/shelf), r (river), s (swamp) are explained in the text. Table 3 (characteristics of map units) is too garbled to tie rows to unit symbols, so its textures, mineralogy, colors and coral dates were not recorded. References partly garbled (Colquhoun 1965 and 1974, Cooke 1936, Gohn 1983, Pooser 1965 skipped; some citations truncated). Legend-only symbols (drill-hole localities) not recorded.\nSUBSURFACE: not held: table 3 lists top and base altitudes (m, relative to sea level, e.g. '+5 to -10', '+19 to +14') for each unit and facies, but row labels are garbled (p. 1). Sheet 2 graphic lithologic logs (logs 1-104; asterisked logs on file at SCGS) give approximate altitudes in meters, depths estimated from 5-foot drill stems; unit boundaries are not legible as numbers. Drill-log index by county: 63-64 Williamsburg, 65-70 Georgetown, 71-78 Colleton, 79 Beaufort, 80-93 Dorchester, 94-104 Charleston; grid references on the map's north and west margins. Section distances and unit elevations are not legible. Datum: sea level; surface altitudes from USGS 1:24,000 and 1:62,500 topographic maps.",
